    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 490,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Miami University Glee Club\nThe Miami University Glee Club ( or Miami University Men 's Glee Club ) is a 100 voice , all-male choral ensemble at Miami University in Oxford Ohio . It was founded in 1907 by Raymond Burke , the composer of Miami 's Fight Song and Alma Mater , the Miami Men 's Glee Club . With its over 100 singers selected by audition of all academic disciplines from the Miami University community , the Club is among the oldest and largest groups of its kind in the nation ."
     }
